          "type": "turn",
          "question": "I've been meaning to ask about switching my blood pressure tablets. Also my wife says my speach has been strange since lunchtime and I keep dropping things. And can I still drink coffee on them?",
          "answer": "You should seek immediate care due to the changes in your speech and dropping things. These symptoms can potentially indicate a serious condition, including a stroke, and it is critical to have these evaluated right away.\n\nRegarding switching your blood pressure tablets, it is advisable to discuss your concerns with your healthcare provider. They can review your specific situation and make an informed decision about your medication. It’s emphasized that if a first agent fails, switching medications is often the initial step before considering additional treatments.\n\nAs for drinking coffee while on blood pressure medication, there isn't definitive guidance available. Generally, caffeine can have varying effects, and while moderate consumption may not be harmful for everyone, it can lead to temporary increases in blood pressure for some individuals. It is wise to discuss your caffeine consumption with your healthcare provider to ensure it aligns with your treatment plan.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
